---
title: "object_ownership_transition (Sui Move Concepts: Ownership State Machine)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_created: object::new(ctx) - fresh object created
    q_created --> q_address_owned: transfer::transfer(obj, addr)
    q_created --> q_shared: transfer::share_object(obj)
    q_created --> q_immutable: transfer::freeze_object(obj)
    q_created --> q_wrapped: stored as field in another object

    q_address_owned --> q_address_owned: transfer::transfer(obj, new_addr)
    q_address_owned --> q_wrapped: added as dynamic field
    q_address_owned --> q_immutable: transfer::freeze_object(obj)
    q_address_owned --> q_deleted: object::delete(id)

    q_shared --> q_deleted: object::delete(id)

    q_wrapped --> q_address_owned: removed from parent and transferred
    q_wrapped --> q_deleted: destructured and UID deleted

    q_immutable --> [*]: permanently immutable (terminal state)
    q_deleted --> [*]: permanently deleted (terminal state)

    note right of q_created
        INV-001: Every object starts in created state with fresh UID
    end note

    note right of q_address_owned
        INV-002: Address-owned objects cannot transition to shared
        INV-003: Only owner can initiate transitions from address-owned
    end note

    note right of q_shared
        INV-004: Shared objects cannot become address-owned or immutable
        INV-005: Shared is a one-way transition (except deletion)
    end note

    note right of q_immutable
        INV-006: Immutable is a terminal state - no further transitions
        INV-007: Immutable objects have no owner and anyone can read them
    end note
